Scout4all - Data collection and privacy

Last updated: 2026-10-22

Data controller: Nicola Baldi, nic.baldi@gmail.com


1. What is collected

Match data. Unless you turn it off (see 4), when you scout a match the
program uploads an archive with:

- the match: date, home or away, gender, year and classification of the
  team, maximum number of substitutions;
- each set: the lineup and the scouted events (time, type, evaluation);
- the identifier of the team.

Teams and players appear only as random identifiers, generated on your
computer. The names of players, teams and opponents, and any other text you
type, are never sent. Without the files on your computer the identifiers
cannot be linked to real people: this is pseudonymous data, not anonymous.

Technical data. The upload server records the IP address and the version of
the program in its logs, and keeps the IP address in memory for a short time
to limit the number of requests.

Issue reports. When you send a report from "report an issue", its title and
description, and your name and e-mail address if you type them, are sent to
Linear, the issue tracker of the project.


2. Why

- Statistics on the use of the program and on volleyball scouting.
- Diagnosis of bugs and improvement of the program.
- Aggregate statistics, which can be used in future services of the
  project, also paid ones (e.g. a cloud version).

The data is never sold, nor used to identify you.

Issue reports are used only to handle the report and to answer you.


3. Legal basis

Match and technical data: the legitimate interest of the developer in
improving the program and diagnosing its bugs (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR), on
pseudonymous data, with your right to object at any time (see 4).

Issue reports: your request. You send them yourself; name and e-mail are
optional.


4. Your choice

The program shows this notice when it starts for the first time. You can
turn the upload of match data off there, or at any time in the settings
(F2, "send match statistics"). Turned off, nothing more is uploaded; to
delete what was already sent, see 7.


5. Where

- Upload server: Render, Frankfurt (EU).
- Match archives: Supabase Storage, Ireland (EU).
- Issue reports: Linear (USA), under its data protection terms.


6. How long

Match archives are kept with no time limit, for statistical purposes
(Art. 5(1)(e) and 89 GDPR): they are pseudonymous and hold no names.
Server logs are kept for the limited time the hosting provider keeps them.
Issue reports are kept as long as needed to handle them.


7. Your rights

You can ask to access, correct or delete your data, or object to its
processing, by writing to nic.baldi@gmail.com. Since the data holds no
names, to find it we need the identifier of your team: the name of its
folder in the ".scout4all" folder of your home directory.

You can also lodge a complaint with a data protection authority (in Italy,
the Garante per la protezione dei dati personali).
